      "name": "DestructorVectorIterator",
      "signature": "void DestructorVectorIterator(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Exception-safe vector destructor iterator for cleaning up object arrays.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Passes vtable pointer (0x04356e70) to identify object type\n2. Specifies element size of 0x28 (40 bytes) for array stride calculation\n3. Specifies element count of 0x17 (23 objects) to destroy\n4. Calls _eh_vector_destructor_iterator_ with destructor function pointer (FUN_0426f590)\n5. Returns to caller\n\nPurpose: \nThis function implements the C++ exception-safe destructor pattern for cleaning up dynamically allocated object arrays. It ensures each of the 23 objects in the array is properly destroyed using the provided destructor function, with proper exception handling during cleanup.\n\nParameters:\nNone - all parameters passed directly to eh_vector_destructor_iterator\n\nReturns:\nvoid - no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Element count is hardcoded to 23 objects\n- Element size is hardcoded to 40 bytes\n- Uses exception handling mechanism for safe cleanup during unwinding\n- Vtable pointer 0x04356e70 identifies the object class being destructed",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:4d9eb45182c1101d050115bd954de8af",
