      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Cleanup ItemDescLookupCache at program termination\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global cache root pointer from DAT_043559f0\n2. Verify cache is not NULL before cleanup\n3. Free internal node list at offset +0x8 by calling FUN_042cdcc0\n4. Free item descriptor strings by calling FUN_042cde90\n5. Deallocate cache root structure via FreeMemory\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone - This is an atexit() handler registered at program initialization (04266050)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If DAT_043559f0 is NULL, skip all cleanup operations and return immediately\n- Used as C runtime atexit() handler for automatic cleanup at program exit\n- Called once during program shutdown after all application logic completes\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type            Description\n------  ----  ---------------      ----            -----------------\n0x0     0x8   [root data]          undefined8      Root hash tree data\n0x8     0x4   pNodeList            Node*           Pointer to linked list of nodes\n0xC     0x4   [capacity/version]   uint            Capacity or version tracking\n0x10+   0x1C  [reserved]           undefined[28]   Reserved/padding space",
