      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Cleanup handler registered with atexit() to process data structures before program termination.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Register this function as program exit handler via atexit() call from FUN_04267100\n2. Load address of global process data (0x435b708) into ECX register\n3. Call FUN_0426f7e0 with process data address as first parameter\n4. FUN_0426f7e0 processes the data structure (typically cleanup/finalization)\n5. Return to allow program termination\n\nParameters:\nNone - this is an atexit handler with no parameters\n\nReturns:\nvoid - standard exit handler signature\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This function is registered as a program exit handler and is called automatically\n- The constant address 0x435b708 refers to global process data (g_ProcessDataPtr)\n- Used with __stdcall calling convention and RET 0x0 (caller cleanup)\n- Similar atexit registrations appear in FUN_04267100 for program initialization",
