      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Wrapper for C++ exception handling vector destructor iteration.\n\nThis function calls the exception handling vector destructor iterator to\ndestroy all elements in a C++ vector during exception unwinding or cleanup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Prepare destructor parameters on stack (base address, element size, count, function pointer)\n2. Call eh_vector_destructor_iterator to iterate through vector elements\n3. Call destructor function on each 28-byte element\n4. Return from wrapper\n\nParameters:\nNone (uses implicit global data)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This is a destructor wrapper that executes during exception handling or cleanup\n- Processes 160 (0xa0) elements of size 28 (0x1c) bytes each\n- Total data size: 160 * 28 = 4480 bytes\n- Called via data reference from initialization code\n- Part of C++ runtime exception handling infrastructure",
