      "name": "CleanupDynamicBuffer",
      "signature": "void CleanupDynamicBuffer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "atexit handler that safely frees a dynamically allocated buffer with corruption detection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if buffer pointer (DAT_0435b7ac) is NULL; exit if so\n2. Call validation function FUN_042ee050 with buffer pointer and size\n3. Calculate aligned size: (end - start) & 0xfffffffc, must be >= 0x1000 (4KB)\n4. If size valid, retrieve allocation base from header at offset -4\n5. Verify allocation metadata: (start - base - 4) must be <= 31 bytes\n6. If metadata invalid, call CorruptionDetected (non-returning error handler)\n7. Free the allocation at base address via FreeMemory\n8. Clear all three global tracking variables to NULL/0\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value, atexit handler)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Allocation is expected to have 4-byte metadata header at offset -4 (allocation base)\n- Minimum allocation size check: 0x1000 (4KB), prevents freeing corrupted/tiny allocations\n- Metadata validation: offset difference must be <= 31 bytes, detects header overruns\n- CorruptionDetected is non-returning (calls abort or similar)",
